::ENG3_U05_L01_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.L.01] Draft: The mural preserves history it shows neighborhood stores and family recipes. Which revision fixes the run-on sentence? {
~The mural preserves history, it shows neighborhood stores and family recipes.#This is a comma splice because two complete thoughts are joined only by a comma.
=The mural preserves history because it shows neighborhood stores and family recipes.#Correct. The revision creates one clear sentence with a logical connection.
~Because the mural preserves history and shows neighborhood stores and family recipes.#This is a fragment because it does not complete the thought.
~The mural preserving history it shows stores and recipes.#This is not a complete, correctly punctuated sentence.
}
::ENG3_U05_L01_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.L.01] Draft: Because the author repeats the image of the locked gate. Which revision makes the fragment complete? {
~Because the author repeats the image.#This is still a fragment.
~Repeating the image of the locked gate.#This is still incomplete.
~The author repeats.#This is complete but loses the analytical meaning.
=The author creates emphasis by repeating the image of the locked gate.#Correct. This sentence has a subject, verb, and complete thought.
}
::ENG3_U05_L01_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.W.04] Draft: The source says the setting is a big deal. Which revision improves academic vocabulary? {
=The source clarifies the setting's symbolic importance.#Correct. This uses precise academic vocabulary.
~The source says the setting matters a lot.#This is clearer but still informal.
~The source is about the setting being big.#This is vague and awkward.
~The source tells setting stuff.#This is informal and unclear.
}
::ENG3_U05_L01_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Passage: The source explains that transit spaces can represent movement and connection. Which paraphrase is clearest and grammatically correct? {
~Transit spaces movement and connection because representation.#This is not a correct sentence.
~Transit places are about things moving and connected and it is shown.#This is vague and grammatically weak.
=Places connected to travel can symbolize movement and human connection.#Correct. This is an accurate paraphrase in standard English.
~Movement and connection is what transit spaces do in literature.#This has subject-verb agreement problems and imprecise wording.
}
::ENG3_U05_L01_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.V.01] Draft: The image is important, it develops memory. Which revision uses correct punctuation and academic language? {
~The image is important, it develops memory.#This is a comma splice.
=The image is significant because it develops the theme of memory.#Correct. This fixes the sentence boundary and uses academic vocabulary.
~The image, significant because memory.#This is a fragment.
~The image is important and memory stuff.#This is informal and unclear.
}
